{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the Rust `cdylib` in [Cargo.toml](/tmp/harvest-translate-ryfoqh/translated_rust/Cargo.toml) and [src/lib.rs](/tmp/harvest-translate-ryfoqh/translated_rust/src/lib.rs). The port preserves the C ABI and exports the same public symbols with `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`: logger functions, task-manager functions, and `driver`.\n\nThe implementation intentionally mirrors the original C behavior, including allocation patterns, log formatting, output formatting, environment-variable handling, and the original bugs/lifetime quirks rather than correcting them. I also checked the headers for namespace-renaming macros; none are present here, so the exported symbol names match the source names directly.\n\n`cargo build --release` succeeds. I also built the original C library separately and compared its behavior against the Rust library for representative inputs; stdout, stderr, return values, and log-file contents matched for those cases."}}
